      <Text selectable style={{ color: colors.foregroundMuted, fontSize: 12, lineHeight: 17.4 }}>Each workstream shows its numbers <Text style={{ fontWeight: "600" }}>At</Text> the selected revision and, when a <Text style={{ fontWeight: "600" }}>vs</Text> revision is chosen at the top, a <Text style={{ fontWeight: "600" }}>Change since</Text> row right under them: each change sits below the number it belongs to (Δ = value at the revision − value at the compare revision, same filters and period; the % is relative to the compare value; ±0 = compared and unchanged). In the epic table the change is the second line of each cell. Progress = Jira child issues: <Text style={{ color: "#0ca30c" }}>● Done</Text> · <Text style={{ color: colors.accent }}>● In progress</Text> · To do; the <Text style={{ fontWeight: "600" }}>striped</Text> part of a bar moved since the compare revision (green = newly done, blue = newly in progress). Consumption follows the period and filters above. The workstreams listed are the ones the <Text style={{ fontWeight: "600" }}>Workstreams</Text> toggle and the workstream picker select: by default the ones still open in Jira at the end of the period that used tokens in it (on All time: open now, with usage {options.activeWindow?.[0]?.label ?? "recently"}); with <Text style={{ fontWeight: "600" }}>All</Text>, the open ones without usage, the ones done in Jira that used tokens in the period, and the historical ones follow in their own groups (historical collapsed). A workstream's rows are its labelled Jira epics; a desk (PR review, Adam ad-hoc) has one row per desk workspace or tab. Workstreams start collapsed — open one with its ▸ caret; expand an epic to list its child issues. Inspect a column name for its definition.</Text>
